I was kindly provided with a 4000/90 FLASH upgrade kit, which I unzipped on=
 a linux box and copied the firmware file, COUGAR.SYS, to an AlphaServer ru=
nning OpenVMS 8.3 using binary mode ftp. I then moved the firmware file int=
o the MOM$LOAD directory (there are instructions provided with the firmware=
 describing how to enable the MOP server). It should also be possible to us=
e a Unix (Linux, *BSD etc) to serve this file.

On the VMS box a DIR/FULL COUGAR.SYS should indicate a fixed-512 record fil=
e.

Then the following process is completed on the 4000/90:

>>> b/100 ez


 Bootfile: cougar



-EZA0


                        ****CAUTION****

--- EXECUTING THIS PROGRAM WILL CHANGE YOUR CURRENT ROM ---


Do you really want to continue [Y/N] ? : Y


