I know that this answer is late to the party, but yes, they are DEC TU60 du=
al cassette tape drives. What has not been said is that they were frequentl=
y paired with PDP-11/10s as a cheap assembly language development (and DEC =
Basic) system, running CAPS-11.  For more info on CAPS-11, look here: http:=
//www.avitech.com.au/basic_caps-11/
I first used CAPS-11 when I was an undergrad and my recollection is that th=
ey were very flakey...seemed that every command caused the system cassette =
to cycle wildly, usually resulting in some read errors and one would be for=
