 >brad@heeltoe.com wrote:

>I'm curious if anyone (else) has tried to boot rsts v10.1 using a emulex UC07 mscp scsi controller...
>
>I gen'd a 10.1 system using simh and an ra81 disk and it boot fine.  But when I copy it to a scsi disk on a UC07 controller it won't boot.  It complains about the cluster size.
>
>I'm wondering if this is a problem with the rsts mscp driver and the UC07 or something else.
>
>My goal is to run rsts v10.1 on an 11/23+ with the UC07.
>
The only suggestion that might be useful (but
still does not really solve the problem) is to
attempt to boot RT-11 on the UC07.

I know that a friend booted RT-11 from a
UC07 about ten years ago, but I don't have
any details.

It would probably be useful to attempt to
do so first under SIMH and then using the
UC07.  If RT-11 works under both, then
you know that RSTS/E may have a specific
problem with the cluster size.  If commented
source code for RSTS/E for the MSCP
device driver is available, then that might
help.  If SIMH does not support stepping
through the boot code for the MSCP device
driver, then Ersatz-11 may be useful to help
in that area since it supports a single break
point at any specific code address.  Stepping
through the boot code for the MSCP device
driver under SIMH or Ersatz-11 might help
you to determine where on the actual DEC
hardware the problem might be located.  Since
boot code is difficult to debug without the
support of an ODT or something similar, the
tools on SIMH or Ersatz-11 might help.

If you do find out anything that helps solve the
problem, please let us know.  If anyone else
uses a UC07 in the future, your solution will
be useful.

I have looked at support for "terminals" under
RT-11 (the KED variants) which have more than
24 lines and 132 columns.  There are KED
variants specifically for RSTS/E which you might
want to use if such "terminals" are available to you
and you want to use the KED editor.

Jerome Fine

